1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,752
[BEA] <i>Why did you come here?</i>

2
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:05,130
<i>You know it's dangerous.</i>

3
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:06,589
[CALOY] <i>'Bi. Are you okay?</i>

4
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,843
<i>Caloy, I don't understand.</i>

5
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:13,221
<i>I want Billy's life</i>
<i>because it should've been mine.</i>

6
00:00:13,304 --> 00:00:15,807
<i>Billy just had to steal it!</i>

7
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,350
<i>I'll help you.</i>

8
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:20,729
<i>I'm here for you.</i>

9
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:24,649
<i>I'm right here.</i>

10
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:31,156
<i>You already have your own life.</i>

11
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>As for Oliver, in a few years,</i>
<i>he'll be going abroad,</i>

12
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:41,624
<i>and he'll be moving out too.</i>

13
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:46,838
<i>So then I thought,</i>
<i>maybe I need to have a life of my own.</i>

14
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:51,718
<i>Do you know whose love story</i>
<i>I'm most excited about?</i>

15
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:54,304
<i>Yours.</i>

16
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:58,558
<i>Because you're someone</i>
<i>who gives so, so much love.</i>

17
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:02,228
<i>So I'm sure you'll get</i>
<i>so, so much love in return.</i>

18
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:06,232
[JORDAN]<i> Bea's mom's name</i>
<i>is Mariela Mercado.</i>

19
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:10,737
<i>She was confined for three years</i>
<i>in a mental institution.</i>

20
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,655
[BILLY] <i>That's serious, Jordan.</i>

21
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:14,532
[JORDAN]<i> But there's nothing</i>
<i>we can do right now</i>

22
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:16,993
<i>except be careful.</i>

23
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:24,125
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

24
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,311
[BILLY] <i>Auntie Pres?</i>

25
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:45,563
<i>- Auntie?</i>
<i>- Mm?</i>

26
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:47,190
<i>- Auntie Pres, sorry.</i>
- [PERCIOUS GRUNTS]

27
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:48,775
[PRECIOUS] <i>Mm?</i>

28
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:52,278
<i>A woman has been standing outside</i>
<i>for a while now.</i>

29
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:54,531
<i>Is it Bea?</i>

30
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,368
<i>Hello? Chief?</i>

31
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:00,370
[OFFICER]<i> Ma'am,</i>
<i>are you the one who called earlier?</i>

32
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:02,413
<i>Yes, it's me. Where are you right now?</i>

33
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:03,957
[OFFICER]<i> We're already near, ma'am.</i>

34
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,041
<i>Thank you.</i>

35
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:06,584
<i>Why did you call the police?</i>

36
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,381
All I have is Bea now.

37
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:13,216
My husband abandoned us.

38
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:15,301
My eldest child

39
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:17,428
has passed away already.

40
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:22,600
[SNIFFLES] I won't be able to handle it
if I also lose Bea.

41
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:25,603
Your daughter is the one
who started this mess.

42
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:27,772
Please, have some empathy.

43
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:29,899
She has done nothing wrong.

44
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:32,569
She was just jealous of her sister,

45
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:34,529
so she pretended to be Abi.

46
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:37,407
Ms. Mariela, this isn't just about her
pretending to be Abi.

47
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:39,784
Your daughter had our system hacked

48
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,828
before she even applied to our company.

49
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,663
I hope you understand that.

50
00:02:43,746 --> 00:02:46,457
Don't accuse her of that!

51
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:47,959
You don't have any proof!

52
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:49,210
Wait a minute.

53
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:51,629
How well do you even know your child?

54
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:55,800
We are certain that Bea ordered Caloy
to trespass into our house!

55
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:58,303
My child was hurt
because of their actions!

56
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:01,139
Actually, Caloy and your child
should be in prison!

57
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,348
Liar!

58
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:06,561
I understand that as a mother,
you just want to protect your child.

59
00:03:06,644 --> 00:03:08,229
But what she's doing is wrong.

60
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:10,523
And as parents,

61
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:12,525
shouldn't we teach our children
to do what's right?

62
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:14,861
We shouldn't be covering up for them.

63
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:17,155
But here you are, lying for your child!

64
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:20,074
What are you trying to say?
That I'm a bad mother?

65
00:03:20,158 --> 00:03:21,993
I didn't say that.

66
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,915
Billy, you're already rich!

67
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:29,626
Your life is so good!

68
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:31,836
But my daughter…

69
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,671
She just asked for help.

70
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:36,216
She made some small mistakes.

71
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:38,051
And you already want her to go to jail?

72
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:41,471
[MARIELA WHIMPERS]

73
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:43,431
Don't you have a heart?

74
00:03:44,182 --> 00:03:48,102
You have no empathy!
Not even a little bit.

75
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:51,522
We're just asking for some compassion.

76
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:53,691
Just some compassion.

77
00:03:54,776 --> 00:04:00,365
Please have some mercy and empathy, Billy.

78
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:03,534
I'm sorry, but I really can't
overlook Abi's actions.

79
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:06,329
Well, aren't you just a damn bastard?!

80
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:08,206
You're so full of yourself!

81
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:10,583
Your life will change, you bastard!

82
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,960
You'll become poor too!

83
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:13,044
You'll suffer!

84
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:15,171
- You should go.
- Auntie Pres, let's go inside.

85
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:16,756
- Please, go home.
- Stay here, Billy.

86
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,716
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]
- The police are here.

87
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,219
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

88
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:24,055
- Stay here, Billy.
- [BILLY] Come on. Go home.

89
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,308
Chief?

90
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:29,435
Chief, we don't want any more trouble.

91
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:32,021
You're the ones messing
with my daughter, right?!

92
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,606
Will you stop her or not?

93
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:36,859
Your child caused trouble. Sir, go on.

94
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,362
Did I trespass? Did I hurt you?!

95
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:42,532
The next time you come here,
I won't be as nice.

96
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,703
Chief, just make sure
she gets home safely.

97
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,413
That's all. Auntie, let's go.

98
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:50,164
Let's go, ma'am.

99
00:04:56,087 --> 00:04:57,213
Let's go.

100
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:09,183
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,813
[MUSIC FADES]

102
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:21,362
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:00,693
Sir, thank you so much.

104
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:03,529
I didn't know my mom had left.
I was so worried.

105
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:05,448
Luckily, she's fine.

106
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:09,077
Thank you for looking for her
and bringing her home.

107
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,661
Thank you so much.

108
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:15,208
We've already warned your mother
not to go to Benilda Cariño's house again.

109
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:20,463
You should consider yourselves lucky
that she didn't escalate the matter.

110
00:06:20,546 --> 00:06:22,090
Because if she had,

111
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:24,342
your mother could've been charged
with unjust vexation.

112
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:26,594
I'm sorry, sir. I'm really sorry.

113
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:30,515
Be sure to keep an eye on your mother
so that it doesn't happen again.

114
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:32,141
Yes, sir.

115
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,935
Again, I'm sorry.
I really am.

116
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,771
- We'll be on our way, ma'am.
- Thank you.

117
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:38,981
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

118
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,525
[CAR DOORS OPENING]

119
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:43,736
[CAR DOORS CLOSING]

120
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:50,993
People like her…

121
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:53,162
They may be delusional.

122
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:57,166
They believe in their own version
of the truth.

123
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,460
[BILLY] <i>Maybe in her eyes,</i>

124
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:01,879
Abi hasn't done anything wrong.

125
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,214
Bea, I mean.

126
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:07,927
It's possible she doesn't really know.

127
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:10,888
But that still doesn't change the fact

128
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:13,724
Bea has to pay for what she did.

129
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:15,017
Absolutely.

130
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:18,229
Do you want me to go there?

131
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:20,606
No need. I'm okay, dude.

132
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:21,732
Thank you.

133
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,985
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:28,322
Wish me luck actually
falling asleep tonight.

135
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:30,491
I'll stay with you.

136
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:33,244
Huh?

137
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:35,037
You want to fall asleep?

138
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:38,583
[SOFT THUD]

139
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:44,005
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

140
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:47,008
[EXHALES] Okay.

141
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:49,760
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

142
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:53,931
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

143
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:56,058
[STRUMMING GUITAR]

144
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:59,228
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

145
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:03,274
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

146
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:05,610
<i>♪ Oh, baby ♪</i>

147
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:10,656
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

148
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:14,744
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

149
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,622
<i>♪ When I found you ♪</i>

150
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:19,957
<i>♪ Everything changed ♪</i>

151
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,335
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

152
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:26,047
<i>♪ Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

153
00:08:27,673 --> 00:08:29,133
It's beautiful.

154
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:31,594
Mommy's composition.

155
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:34,680
[STRUMMING CONTINUES]

156
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:37,892
[JADE SINGING]
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

157
00:08:37,975 --> 00:08:42,188
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

158
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:46,108
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

159
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:50,696
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

160
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,073
<i>♪ Oh, baby ♪</i>

161
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:56,410
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

162
00:08:56,494 --> 00:09:00,623
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

163
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:06,045
<i>♪ Do you know? When I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed ♪</i>

164
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:09,173
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

165
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:13,427
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

166
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:17,848
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

167
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:20,643
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you ♪</i>

168
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:23,145
<i>♪ Everything changed ♪</i>

169
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:25,064
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

170
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:29,068
<i>♪ Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

171
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:30,361
[STRUMMING GUITAR]

172
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:33,114
<i>♪ I'm coming home ♪</i>

173
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:34,991
- [SQUEALS]
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

174
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:36,409
- [SMOOCHES]
- [GIGGLING]

175
00:09:36,492 --> 00:09:38,369
<i>Good morning. </i>[GIGGLES]

176
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:42,873
[JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

177
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:47,503
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

178
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:48,754
[STRUMMING GUITAR]

179
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:51,424
[HUMMING]

180
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:55,803
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

181
00:09:55,886 --> 00:10:00,308
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

182
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,936
[HUMMING]

183
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,565
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

184
00:10:07,648 --> 00:10:09,233
<i>♪ Because ♪</i>

185
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:11,986
<i>♪ I'm coming home ♪</i>

186
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:20,911
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:26,042
[MUSIC BECOMES BRIGHT]

188
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,924
[MUSIC FADING]

189
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:42,600
[MARIELA SNIFFLES]

190
00:10:47,229 --> 00:10:49,315
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

191
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:50,399
Ma…

192
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,693
Ma, look at me.

193
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:55,571
Please, don't do that again.

194
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,031
Just don't.

195
00:10:57,114 --> 00:10:59,992
Remember what I told you? I'll find a way.

196
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:00,951
Okay?

197
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:02,328
I just…

198
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:05,539
I can't bear to see you suffer, my dear.

199
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:07,667
Me? Suffering?

200
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:08,918
I'm not suffering.

201
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,753
I never said I was suffering.

202
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:12,004
I'll find a way.

203
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:14,048
I'll get a job and then…

204
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:16,258
I'll get back at Billy.

205
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:17,468
I promise you.

206
00:11:17,551 --> 00:11:19,220
I'll make her pay.

207
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:20,888
- [SNIFFLES]
- [SIGHS]

208
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:23,682
Don't cry anymore.
Take your medicine, Ma.

209
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,935
[MARIELA SNIFFLING]

210
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:28,270
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

211
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,939
- [SNIFFLES]
- Are you okay, Ma?

212
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:33,234
[SNIFFLING]

213
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:35,653
Are you okay?

214
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,947
[MARIELA SNIFFLING]

215
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:43,619
[SOBBING]

216
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,331
[BEA SHUSHING]

217
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:51,710
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:54,713
- [SNIFFLES, SOBS]
- [SHUSHING]

219
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,392
- [MUSIC ENDS]
- [BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

220
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:13,691
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

221
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:18,195
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

222
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,321
- [GASPS]
- [MUSIC STOPS]

223
00:12:21,031 --> 00:12:23,451
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:24,618
[SIGHS]

225
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:28,706
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

226
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:37,590
[LINE RINGING]

227
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:39,842
Hello, dude?

228
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:42,428
Could you come with me?

229
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:47,516
Will you watch me again, Auntie?

230
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,937
Of course! I'm making the most of our time
together before you go to Kingsley.

231
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:53,105
[OLIVER GROANS SOFTLY]

232
00:12:54,231 --> 00:12:57,943
- But, Auntie, they're staring.
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

233
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:00,613
[STUDENT] He's such an attention-seeker.

234
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:03,199
Don't mind them!

235
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:05,493
It's nice your auntie's always here.

236
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:08,162
- [PRECIOUS] Hm.
- Hmm…

237
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:11,540
All right, Sir Eric, Auntie,
I'll get going now.

238
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:13,417
Love you!

239
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:15,669
- [HUSHED] Love you!
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES]

240
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:21,258
Oliver's lucky to have you.

241
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:24,887
Oh, I'm the one who's lucky
to have him and his sister.

242
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:36,565
No! No! Let me go! No! No! No!

243
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:39,485
Let me go! No! No!

244
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:45,241
Miss, is there really no way we can look
at Mariela Mercado's files?

245
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:48,077
I'm really sorry, ma'am, but you can't.

246
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,745
Those are confidential.

247
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,539
I'm sorry.

248
00:13:52,581 --> 00:13:53,707
Okay.

249
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,293
- Excuse me.
- [BILLY] Okay.

250
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:02,508
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:05,135
[WOMAN] Nurse, get them inside.

252
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:14,853
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:16,105
No.

254
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:17,606
Jordan, my God.

255
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,025
- Stay here.
- Jordan!

256
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:22,653
- Keep watch for me.
- Shh!

257
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:40,713
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

258
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:58,105
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:01,108
Hey.

260
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:08,073
Okay, make sure of it. Watch her well.

261
00:15:13,787 --> 00:15:15,247
Miss!

262
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:18,417
I really cannot allow it!

263
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:22,087
I haven't even said anything!

264
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:23,505
It's not allowed.

265
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:26,800
You need either a doctor's request
or a warrant.

266
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,557
Miss, if it had been up to me,

267
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:36,060
I wouldn't have traveled all the way here.

268
00:15:36,143 --> 00:15:38,312
I mean, traffic's very bad these days!

269
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:39,939
Oh, that's true.

270
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:50,491
And fuel prices have increased again!
My gosh!

271
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:53,786
- Even my child's school fees.
- The expenses!

272
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:55,079
The expenses, everything!

273
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:58,082
[BILLY] Even electricity!
Everything's getting pricier!

274
00:15:58,165 --> 00:15:59,625
- [NURSE] That's true.
- [BILLY] Right?

275
00:15:59,708 --> 00:16:01,710
My gosh, it's never-ending!

276
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:04,838
And the-- This! It's so hot!

277
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:07,549
It's so hot, but then it'll suddenly rain!

278
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:08,759
[NURSE] It's even getting dark.

279
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:10,511
[BILLY] I know! It might rain soon.

280
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:13,597
- That's why we have to go.
- [NURSE] Is that so?

281
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:14,765
We might get caught in the rain.

282
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:16,517
- I'm sorry for the trouble.
- [NURSE] It's fine.

283
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:19,395
- Take care! Okay.
- Okay.

284
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:21,855
- [NURSE] Take care!
- [BILLY] Come on, baby!

285
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,150
Bye!

286
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:26,819
- [JORDAN] Babe.
- [BILLY CHUCKLING]

287
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:30,155
That couple is so weird.

288
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:33,450
According to the employer of the real Abi,

289
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:37,538
they've had no more contact
with the family after the fire.

290
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:40,833
Did you know that her mother
has a burn scar on her head?

291
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:45,879
Maybe she was also there during the fire.

292
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,882
But it still doesn't explain

293
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:51,427
Bea's huge grudge against you.

294
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:54,763
I hope we finally learn why.

295
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:58,267
We need to find out right away, Jordan.

296
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:00,352
My family's safety is at stake here.

297
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:01,979
We will.

298
00:17:02,062 --> 00:17:06,025
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

299
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:08,360
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

300
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:13,198
[CAR ENGINE HUMMING]

301
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,336
Is this the right address?

302
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:30,007
29 Evangeline Street, Valencia.

303
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,303
This is the place.

304
00:17:34,386 --> 00:17:35,888
This was Bea's old house.

305
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:43,687
[STIRRING MUSIC BUILDS]

306
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:52,654
[STIRRING MUSIC SLOWLY FADES]

307
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:56,200
Fernando Castillo owns that house now.

308
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:58,952
Where is he now? Do you have any records?

309
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:00,370
Oh, he's dead.

310
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:04,708
None of his relatives have come here
to claim the property either.

311
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:07,795
Was the previous owner of the house
Mariela Mercado?

312
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:09,088
Mercado?

313
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,631
I don't think so.

314
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:11,924
- Hold on.
- [KEYBOARD CLANKING]

315
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,509
It's not here either.

316
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:19,014
We just moved here,
so the records aren't complete yet.

317
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,390
But wait…

318
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:24,770
I think Mr. Castillo mentioned
someone before.

319
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:26,063
Mariela?

320
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,982
That's the name I remember.

321
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,277
Do you know what caused the fire?

322
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:34,988
No one knows, miss.

323
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:38,450
All I heard was that Mariela survived.

324
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,244
And so did her youngest daughter.

325
00:18:40,327 --> 00:18:42,579
But her eldest daughter died.

326
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:44,414
To be honest,

327
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:47,501
hardly anyone ever inquires
about that property.

328
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,294
Besides being supposedly unlucky,

329
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:51,755
there's a huge problem with the title.

330
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:56,176
That's why I don't think Mr. Castillo
ever finished paying the seller.

331
00:18:56,260 --> 00:19:02,266
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

332
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:05,102
When did the fire happen?

333
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:09,439
About 12 or 13 years ago, I think.

334
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:12,109
Do you know what happened
to the youngest daughter

335
00:19:12,192 --> 00:19:13,318
of the house's former owner?

336
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,237
As far as I know,

337
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:18,198
she took her mother
to Manila for treatment.

338
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:24,329
<i>Oh! So we're in the same boat,</i>
<i>Ms. Billy Idol!</i>

339
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,207
<i>I told you before, right?</i>

340
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:31,712
<i>I don't have a father.</i>
<i>My sister's gone too.</i>

341
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:34,006
<i>It's just my mother and me.</i>

342
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:36,592
But the father wasn't with them?

343
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:38,802
No, he wasn't.

344
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:42,806
The rumor is that
Mariela's husband left her.

345
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:45,767
Wait, why are you asking about them?

346
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:47,186
Hmm…

347
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:49,813
Auntie Mariela is my aunt.

348
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:51,356
Oh, I see.

349
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:55,777
Sorry, but we don't really know
anything else about them.

350
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:58,030
They weren't from around here either.

351
00:19:58,113 --> 00:20:01,992
And you know, when a family is well-off,
they don't really mingle with others.

352
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:06,914
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

353
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,248
- Thank you.
- All right.

354
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:10,125
- Thank you.
- Okay, sure.

355
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:14,922
[STIRRING MUSIC SWELLS]

356
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:17,341
<i>She lied about her sister.</i>

357
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:19,760
<i>But what she said</i>
<i>about her father?</i>

358
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:21,803
<i>- That seems to be true.</i>
<i>- What's your connection to this?</i>

359
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:25,140
<i>I don't know why</i>
<i>she hates Billy so much,</i>

360
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:28,393
<i>to the point that she even</i>
<i>conspired with a criminal.</i>

361
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,311
<i>A criminal?</i>

362
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:31,271
<i>How long are you going</i>
<i>to keep it hidden?</i>

363
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:33,273
<i>She's going to find out</i>
<i>the truth eventually.</i>

364
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:35,442
<i>If she finds out the truth,</i>

365
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:37,069
<i>Billy's done for.</i>

366
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:39,112
<i>I hope you can</i>
<i>hear me out.</i>

367
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:42,282
<i>I really need a job because--</i>

368
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:43,492
<i>- Hey!</i>
- [GASPS]

369
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:45,619
[MOTORCYCLE ROARING]

370
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:47,829
<i>Sorry for the hassle.</i>

371
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,414
<i>I'm doing this for you.</i>

372
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:53,418
<i>If you go down, we all go down.</i>

373
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:55,671
<i>I have good news.</i>

374
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:59,091
<i>I have a potential sponsor,</i>

375
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:00,008
<i>and it's…</i>

376
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:04,179
<i>Talia & Co., the jewelry brand!</i>
[GIGGLES]

377
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:07,140
<i>They want you to wear this</i>
<i>to the awards night.</i>

378
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:10,519
<i>This necklace costs 30 million.</i>

379
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:14,982
<i>I think she'll make</i>
<i>a wonderful partner for our event.</i>
